   "source": [
    "## 11. Data integration and join validation\n",
    "\n",
    "The app catalog and review table are related through `App`, but their row grains differ. There are many reviews per app. The review rows are therefore grouped to one row per app before merging. The summary includes the number of usable reviews, mean sentiment polarity and subjectivity, and the shares of positive, negative, and neutral labels.\n",
    "\n",
    "The app analysis table has one row per app name and the review summary has one row per app name. A one-to-one left merge should preserve the app row count. Merge indicators report matched and unmatched app names. Review-only app names are also counted with an outer merge. An integration plan records table grain, key, relationship, and join decision before merging.\n",
    "\n",
    "Exact duplicate review rows are reported, but they are not silently removed. Since repeated text can be a real repeated observation or a data issue, the summarized results are described as review-row summaries from this supplied file."
   ]
  },
