   "source": [
    "## 14. Empirical rule demonstration\n",
    "\n",
    "The real app variables do not provide a clear, approximately normal measurement for this demonstration. Ratings are bounded and installs are strongly skewed. The notebook therefore uses a clearly labelled normal simulation with a fixed seed.\n",
    "\n",
    "For a bell-shaped distribution, the empirical rule expects about 68% of values within one standard deviation of the mean, about 95% within two, and about 99.7% within three. The simulated percentages are calculated from the generated values and compared with these reference levels."
   ]
