  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "6a1f6af2",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "The percentages should be close to 68%, 95%, and 99.7%, with small differences expected in a finite sample. The rule describes a roughly bell-shaped distribution and should not be assumed for highly skewed or multi-peaked data.\n",
    "\n",
